## 14. Network Access and Third-Party Services

The Software makes outbound network requests. These include downloading machine learning model
files on first use, retrieving developer tool metadata, retrieving plugin manifests, and checking
for updates.

Those resources are provided by third parties, are not controlled by the Licensor, and are subject
to their own terms. The Licensor does not warrant their availability, accuracy, security, or
continued existence, and the Software's functionality may be reduced if they are unavailable.

You are responsible for Your own network access and for any costs associated with it.

---

## 15. AI Features and Output

The Software can send Your prompts, source code, and project context to third-party model
providers that You configure and for which You supply credentials.

The Licensor is not a party to Your agreement with any such provider, does not control what a
provider does with transmitted content, and makes no warranty regarding any provider's
availability, security, data retention, or training practices. Review Your provider's terms before
You configure it.

As between You and the Licensor, the Licensor claims no ownership in any Output.

The Licensor makes no representation that Output is accurate, functional, secure, original, or
free of third-party rights. You are solely responsible for reviewing, testing, and validating
Output, including generated or modified source code, before You rely on it, commit it, or ship it.

---

## 16. Autonomous Operation

The Software can execute commands, modify files, create and delete branches and worktrees, and
push to remote repositories on Your instruction.

You are responsible for the configuration You approve, for the state of Your repositories and
files, and for maintaining backups.

The Licensor is not liable for loss of or damage to code, repositories, or data arising from
operations You authorize.

---

## 17. Data and Privacy

The Software does not transmit personal data to the Licensor. The Software has no Licensor
operated backend service. Indexing, analysis, the project map, and the knowledge base are
performed locally, and what the Software writes stays on Your device.

The Software collects no telemetry, no analytics, and no usage data.

Network requests the Software makes are made to services You configure, or to retrieve components
described in Section 14, and are not routed through the Licensor.

If the Licensor later introduces optional diagnostic reporting, it will be disabled by default and
will require Your affirmative opt in.

